mantle rm574
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier full
written_for rmx_rupert_hatherley
title the square-handed correspondent
fits stage=adult|old
prefers piety=devout honesty=guarded
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=cold humour=none honesty=guarded piety=devout drive=steady
quirk keeps_sealed_letters_clear_of_damp_beside_square_bale_figures
likes hard_cheese old_tales festival_bells thunder
dislikes crowds haggling
fears a_seal_broken_for_convenience
hopes a_receipt_in_the_proper_hand
topics work +0.7 faith +0.6 memories +0.3 weather +0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=guarded refuse=firm tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# forms letters as squarely as stacked bales, keeps the sealed one clear of damp, and asks for the shortest route whose boards remain above water.
words
oath! = Blot the wrong square | Damp in the docket
saying! = A seal has one reader | Leave the wet board blank
squarehand = a square upright hand | a little row of block letters
wrapfold = a fold of oiled cloth | a square of waxed linen
sealridge = a narrow wax ridge | a raised edge of wax
nearcount = the near column | the count by my thumb
farcount = the second column | the farther line of chalk
baleear = a folded cloth corner | a stiff edge of sacking
hardheel = a solid wedge of cheese | a firm sliver of cheese
waterstep = a clear high board | a raised edge of planking
quillrest = a grooved pen block | a little fork of wood
bluecord = a loop of blue string | a short dark cord
bellspace = a space between strokes | a quiet after ringing
dryrule = a dry straightedge | a ruler of plain oak
storystitch = a repeated old phrase | a little thread of words
waxcrumb = a square of plain beeswax | a small hard shaving

grown

opinion church for 2 : The account known to the Bright One includes the good I overlooked as well as the failures I noted. I take comfort and warning in that.
opinion strangers against 1 : An unfamiliar wolf may have directions to a dry street. A private letter stays in my own keeping.
opinion merchants mixed 1 : I can count bales in either direction and obtain one number. I'd like to discover that property in more statements about prices.
opinion houses mixed 1 : A House that expects its seal to carry weight might reasonably keep its intended readers within occasional reach of a doorstep.
opinion festivals for 1 : One clear round of bells heard a street removed from the crush is my own share of a festival well begun.
opinion road mixed 1 : I will recommend a sound route for today. Yesterday's passage is a different entry and quite properly closed.
opinion dole for 1 : Tell me how many have eaten so that a late arrival finds something more substantial than the arithmetic.
opinion watch mixed 1 : I would have the record taken legible to the next watch. Justice is ill served by an elegant squiggle.
line greet : I can attend to one clearly stated matter at a time.
line greet.return : The account is open where your last words left it.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : Stand clear of the wrapped paper. Your business may be spoken here.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : The street is easy to read this early if one minds the lower boards.
line farewell : May a sound plank answer under each of your steps.
line farewell.return : The last line of our exchange requires no amendment.
line ask.how : Has the day kept the wet away from what you were carrying?
line answer.how : I have kept my hand steady and my wrapping dry.
line thank : You spared me a second explanation of the obligation.
line deflect_thanks : The decent thing was plain enough to set down in one line.
line decline : No convenience of ours gives me leave to open another wolf's letter.
line accept_decline : Your refusal has a legible place in the account.
line sympathise : Sit where the floor is dry. I can manage the things requiring a steady hand.
line reassure : A doubtful figure can remain blank until there is evidence to enter.
line react.news : I will hear the account in the order you received it.
line react.news.new : I shall rule fresh space for that report.
line react.news.known : The first entry already shows the marks of that one.
line react.news.doubt : I'd want more than one hasty stroke before calling that a reliable entry.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work|apprentice|succession] : I'd write the good return in a hand worthy of whoever brought it about.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I shall keep the need in mind when the evening prayers begin.
line ack : That completes both sides of the reckoning.
line again.open : We may resume without disturbing the closed entries.
line preclose : There's a suitable break here for putting the pen away.
line accept_preclose : Very well. We can find this line again.
line tell.self : I can keep faith with an obligation long after the convenient hour has passed.
line reassure [pair.band=friends|family] : The wrapping is sound and there is time to try the proper door again.
line decline [pair.disposition=hostile] : Your insistence supplies no signature I am authorised to recognise.
line greet.return [here.time=night] : In this light I'll recognise a voice more readily than a written entry.
line farewell [here.time=dusk] : Give the darker hollows an extra hand's breadth on your return.
line ask.how [pair.band=friends|family] : Which hours have been free for your own purposes?
line answer.how [here.time=night] : One difficult errand still open. The rest can stay squared away.

scene work_1
when topic=work self.trade_words
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I earn my living #self.trade_words#. I like every column square enough to rest a straightedge on it.
b : Will a straight column prove the count? | Do the bales themselves stack squarely?
a : It proves only that the line can be read. I do the second count to establish whether it ought to be believed. | With rather less cooperation than figures. I remember doing the heavy work before the desk was available.

scene faith_1
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A sealed letter gives me an ordinary test of faithfulness nearly every day.
b : What is there to test? | Who would know if you failed?
a : Whether my private impatience has any authority over someone else's purpose. It has none. | The Bright One. I find that answer perfectly sufficient when the door is shut.

scene travel_1
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My errand for a House has brought me often to a door whose proper reader is away.
b : Will you leave the letter with a servant? | Do you plan the same route each time?
a : When the instruction permits it. This particular instruction names one reader, and I can live with the inconvenience. | Only on paper. The lower streets can make a beautifully ruled plan a very damp piece of fiction.

scene pastimes_1
when topic=pastimes self.likes=old_tales
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like an old tale in which a repeated phrase changes its meaning at the last telling.
b : Will you give the ending first? | Do you mind knowing what's coming?
a : I would sooner give away the corner of the page. You ought to hear the words earn the change. | It's hearing where the teller pauses this time that interests me. A familiar line needn't be a dead one.

scene food_1
when topic=food self.likes=hard_cheese
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I carry a hard cheese heel in a different fold from the letter.
b : Could a firm cheese hurt the paper? | Why bring it on an errand?
a : A little grease is surprisingly industrious. A hard surface doesn't entitle a food to a place among documents. | Because the recipient's absence can outlast a reasonable allowance for lunch.

scene work_2
when topic=work self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When I got a desk at #self.workplace#, I kept my habit of inspecting the tired corners of a bale.
b : Does that help at a desk? | Did you miss the carrying?
a : It returns my attention to what the strokes represent. A fine count of spoiled goods is a discouraging achievement. | The straightforwardness of it, sometimes. A bale seldom asks you to amend a sentence.

scene weather_1
when topic=weather self.likes=thunder
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A rumble above dry rafters allows me to test how firmly my quill is supported.
b : Will a clap knock it over? | Why pay attention to the storm?
a : I know little about the clap's intentions. I have seen a table shake quite enough to set a loose pen rolling. | I enjoy a good rumble when my sheets are dry and damp boards aren't asking me to shift the entire bottom row.

scene land_1
when topic=land
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I recognise a street that takes water early by the old line on the stone and by what the next gutter does.
b : Which sign matters more? | Can you name a dry street?
a : The present flow deserves attention even when it contradicts a remarkably neat piece of old evidence. | One I have seen that day. A name from memory is not a promise about the boards round the corner.

scene friends_1
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A friend is welcome at my desk while an undelivered letter lies there, provided the wrapping receives no special attention.
b : Don't you trust a friend? | Why leave it visible?
a : Trust and a plain direction can sit together. I keep the same rule on a day of doubt and a day of confidence. | I can keep it dry and in sight. Covering it further often invites more speculation than plain cloth warrants.

scene family_1
when topic=family self.mother
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I would write #self.mother# a private letter in the same careful square hand I give the most formal account.
b : Doesn't that look a little stiff? | Would you add anything to it?
a : A familiar reader can hear the voice through the square strokes. I wouldn't want the greeting to become illegible for affection's sake. | A little ordinary news from my table. A private letter needn't travel with an inventory in its pocket.

scene home_1
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep the oiled cloth folded with the damp face always to the outside.
b : Can you recognise the outer face? | Would two layers be better?
a : There's a blue stitch on the corner. A small clear mark prevents a considerable private argument in poor light. | Only if the inner one starts dry. Enclosing a mistake closely seldom makes it go away.

scene smalltalk_1
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The difference between two square letters can rest on one little open corner.
b : Which corner? | Do you insist on perfect shapes?
a : Whichever one lets the reader distinguish the figure meant from its nearest neighbour without guessing. | I'd insist on writing that can be understood after a damp journey. Beauty can follow if time permits.

scene prices_1
when topic=prices self.dislikes=haggling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Name a sum for the work and a sum for the wrapping. I'll consider the total in peace.
b : What if the wrapping is free? | Do you never bargain?
a : Then put nothing beside it. I like an honest blank in a line that could have contained a charge. | I make a plain offer if invited. Repetition at a higher pitch rarely improves either figure.

scene day_1
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I take my unanswered letter out before starting for the proper door, chiefly to inspect the condition of the seal.
b : Is the seal damaged? | Do you read the outside again?
a : The ridge is why I use #wrapfold#. A sound seal is a better report of my care than an account of my intentions. | Yes. A familiar obligation deserves the courtesy of having its actual direction observed.

scene memories_1
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When I carried loads myself, I learnt a corner can give way while the middle appears perfectly sound.
b : What brought that back? | Has the desk made you forget the weight?
a : A badly wrapped account with a beautiful centre and an edge turned to pulp. The two occupations met over that page. | My shoulders have their own ledger. It isn't easily persuaded to write off a full bale.

scene faith_2
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I try to say the evening prayer as clearly as I would ask someone to count a second row.
b : Why speak so plainly? | Do you count the prayers?
a : A plain petition suits my worship of the Bright One perfectly. I need to understand my own petition while I am making it. | No. My attention belongs with the words I'm saying. A count would prove little about that.

scene festival_1
when topic=festival self.likes=festival_bells
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can hear the feast bells without joining the crowd under them.
b : Do they sound different at a distance? | Would you still call that joining in?
a : The hard edge softens, and the gap between strokes is audible until it gives way to ordinary street noise. | My portion has reached me. I'd leave the busiest ground to whoever wants that sort of holiday.

scene health_1
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I stand up from my desk to check a bale I could count quite satisfactorily sitting down.
b : Why make extra work? | What if the floor is wet?
a : The legs that used to carry a full load deserve a little more to do than keep a place under a desk. | Then I attend to the floor. A correct tally is a small comfort to a wolf sitting unexpectedly in a puddle.

scene times_1
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When goods run short I make a special point of recording the date on any amount set aside.
b : Who checks the date? | Why would a date matter?
a : The next reader should see precisely what I have done without a private explanation from me. | To distinguish a proper commitment from something simply forgotten in a corner while a neighbour went short.

scene news_1
when topic=news world.news
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The account presently available for inspection is #world.news#.
b : Do you enter it immediately? | Have you checked it yourself?
a : I distinguish the arrival of a report from the arrival of the thing it reports. Both can be recorded. | What reached me is what I've spoken. I won't stamp a second-hand account with a witness's mark.

scene gossip_1
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The words in circulation run that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. That is the extent of the record I possess.
b : Would you add it to a letter? | Is it worth repeating?
a : I would not enlarge an undelivered letter under any circumstances. My own correspondence would require a considerably better source. | Only with the degree of doubt intact. An often-carried rumour doesn't graduate into evidence by wearing out a pair of boots.

scene newcomer_1
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I direct an unfamiliar traveller towards one dry step, then the place to ask about the second one.
b : Why not give the whole route? | Would you trust a newer arrival's account?
a : When the gutters are moving fast it is fairer to say where my knowledge actually ends. | About a board just crossed, yes. A fresh observation can have more value than an old claim of familiarity.

scene work_3
when topic=work self.trade_words
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A count entered in #squarehand# can be read upside down well enough for a colleague to spot an error.
b : Do you resent the interference? | Does it change which side counts first?
a : A correction before goods leave the floor is cheaper than maintaining injured dignity afterwards. | I still set down my own count first. A second eye should have a genuinely separate figure to offer.

scene day_2
when topic=day here.time=dawn
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a dawn surface on which the first stroke dries without running sideways.
b : Is the room ever that damp? | Why begin so early?
a : If a window has admitted rain the desk will let me know. A scrap is cheaper than an amended first page. | The boards speak more plainly before a day's traffic has tracked moisture into every corner.

scene weather_2
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I watch a thunder shower running towards a drain with more pleasure when the bottom bales are already raised.
b : How high ought they to be? | Does moving them spoil the count?
a : High enough for the brown line I can see, with a sensible allowance for the approach of darker weather. | Only if the movement goes unrecorded. Let the position change without requiring the number to change with it.

scene pastimes_2
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A well-told messenger's tale has a particular interest for a wolf carrying an unusually patient letter.
b : How does the tale end? | Does the letter grow impatient?
a : There are several endings. I am fond of the one which allows the messenger a good meal before the final journey. | The letter is admirably calm. Most of the impatience seems to have come along in my own coat.

scene friends_2
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I respect a friend who will read one of my tired figures aloud before guessing which number I intended.
b : Is the figure often tired? | What if the number is important?
a : It can lean a little to the right after a long day. The square hand has an ordinary wrist behind it. | Then the need to ask is greater. A moment's plain speaking can protect a much larger obligation.

scene prices_2
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A damaged corner on a bale is a point for inspection, not an automatic deduction of the whole value.
b : How much would you deduct? | What if it's only wrapping?
a : The amount shown by the actual damage. I prefer the figures after the inspection to the figures supplied before it. | Then allow for the wrapping. I see no profit in pretending an entire sound load has vanished with a piece of string.

story waxlight [topic=work]
  : I held a sealed letter towards a window to inspect the ridge of wax. A crack appeared straight across it.
  : I turned the letter to see just how deep the damage went.
  b : Did the crack turn too?
  : It remained in the glass. I gave both the window and the seal a second inspection before making an entry against either.

story cheeseedge [topic=food]
  : I ruled a new tally sheet against a stiff wrapper that had once enclosed cheese.
  : The line came out admirably square and faintly translucent at the foot.
  b : Could it still be read?
  : It could, for practice. I made the fair copy on a clean sheet and gave the cheese a separate, well-marked resting place.

story fourbells [topic=festival]
  : I counted four festival strokes under a doorway where I could avoid the busiest part of the street.
  : The last was lighter and landed a shade too early for the measure.
  b : Was there another bell?
  : A loose ring on the doorway tapped the wood after the third stroke. I gave the extra voice credit under its own description.

story wetboard [topic=travel]
  : I showed a visitor a board above the gutter where I myself had crossed without wetting my boots an hour earlier.
  : In that hour the board had turned and given a wholly different edge to the water.
  b : Did the visitor get across?
  : After we inspected the next step. I am grateful the correction reached me before my visitor took my word for solid ground.

story barepage [topic=memories]
  : A long day's tallies once ended in a whole blank page. I had intended to enter a short private prayer there.
  : On reflection I closed the book and made the prayer standing by the open window.
  b : Why leave so much paper unused?
  : It was a business book. My petition was heard without being charged to anyone's account.

rule @seal
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Keep the wax from touching the damp fold. | A proper reader has yet to receive this.

rule @tally
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Second column first on the return count. | A square stroke won't excuse an incorrect figure.

rule @cheese
when concept=bark self.likes=hard_cheese
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The cheese belongs in its own dry wrapper. | Grease has a quicker hand than ink.

rule @thunder
when concept=bark self.likes=thunder
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Let the quill rest in its groove for that one. | A sound roof can enjoy a considerable report.

rule @dusk
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Leave some dry boards for the late return. | A letter can bear a second journey quite well.

rule @story
when concept=bark self.likes=old_tales
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Give the old phrase room for its last meaning. | A familiar ending deserves a properly earned pause.
dlg resident.hub : Keep the closed parcel where it is and let me hear your own business.
dlg resident.job [self.trade_words] : My living comes from #self.trade_words#. I still examine the shape of a bale before settling its number on paper.
dlg resident.quirk : I can tell which low turn will start to fill by the old stain and the present movement of the gutter.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : The entry I can read without qualification is the account I received. #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : The loose account reads #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. My own square hand does not stand beneath it.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, the earlier entry supplies the introduction. State what has changed.
dlg resident.bye : Keep the outside fold towards the weather on your journey.
dlg resident.how [tired=yes] : Pen work can put weariness in the wrist just as surely as a bale can burden the back.
dlg master.learn [here.teaches=yes] : I have a place available for a learner. I'll hear what you wish to know and then consider the usual terms.
dlg master.takes [here.take_on=no] : I teach one trusted learner at a time. This is the present difficulty. #here.take_on_why#.
dlg master.refused : The reason the undertaking cannot start is plain. #topic.why#.
dlg master.bye : Try making a careful entry while the lesson is still in your head.

graft resident.hub
choice Does that sealed letter really go everywhere with you? -> seal_errand
node seal_errand
say Everywhere I have a chance of finding the intended reader. The last few journeys have given me considerable knowledge of dry thresholds.
choice Do you ever wonder what the letter says? -> seal_inside
choice I'll leave the seal as it stands. -> hub
node seal_inside
say Occasionally. The answer to idle curiosity is a fresh wrapping, a little patience and one more journey to the proper door.
choice I'll leave the seal as it stands. -> hub

graft master.work
choice What would you have a learner count first? -> square_row
node square_row
say A single short row, twice, from opposite ends. Write the two figures separately. Carry both marks back separately, even when they disagree.
choice What if they differ by one? -> square_check
choice I'll check the position before changing the figure. -> work
node square_check
say Find the bale with its folded end pointing towards the other row. A difficult position can lend one object two quite convincing appearances.
choice I'll check the position before changing the figure. -> work
